course: dictionary
lesson: 2224
title: Covenant: a solemn promise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A covenant is a solemn promise or agreement, a serious promise that people keep. «God made a covenant with Noah» means God made a serious promise with Noah. Solemn means serious and important.
explain: The sentence often gives you the meaning right after the word. «God then set a rainbow in the clouds as a sign of his covenant, a solemn promise, never again to destroy the earth by a flood.» The words «a solemn promise» sit right beside covenant and explain it.
explain: Covenant has two meanings. In the Bible it is a promise between God and people. In law it is a formal written agreement, like a rule in a house deed. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Covenant means a solemn promise or agreement.
fact: In the Bible, God made covenants with Noah, Abraham, Moses and David.
fact: «Covenant» in law means a formal written agreement, such as a promise to give money to a charity.
fact: The rainbow is the sign of God's covenant with Noah.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «make a covenant», «keep the covenant», «the Ark of the Covenant» and «the new covenant».
exercise: «God then set a rainbow in the clouds as a sign of his covenant, a solemn promise.» What is a covenant? | A kind of rainbow | A type of cloud | A flood | *A solemn promise or agreement
exercise: In the Bible, which sign showed God's covenant with Noah? | A bird | A star | A river | *A rainbow
exercise: A builder signs a covenant to protect the land he buys. What kind of covenant is this? | A Bible promise | *A formal written agreement | A dance | A rainbow sign
test: «David danced with joy before God when the Ark of the Covenant was brought to Jerusalem.» In this sentence, the Ark of the Covenant is best described as | *A holy chest linked to God's covenant | A type of lawyer | A rainbow in the sky | A boat that floats on the flood
test: What does «keep the covenant» most likely mean? | *Stay faithful to the promise | Sell the land | Forget the rules | Break the promise
exam: Which clue helps you understand covenant in «God then set a rainbow in the clouds as a sign of his covenant, a solemn promise»? | The word set | The word clouds | *The words a solemn promise right after it | The word rainbow only
